name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-preassessment-q13_2026-pilot'

question 'A student receives feedback on a project from a peer and also from an AI tool. The peer says the conclusion is confusing. The AI says the conclusion is well-written. What should the student do?'

right 'Consider both sources of feedback critically, recognizing that human experience may catch things AI misses.'
wrong 'Always trust the AI because it has read more examples of good writing than the peer.'
wrong 'Ignore the peer\'s feedback since AI tools are always more accurate.'
wrong 'Rewrite the entire project from scratch to be safe.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

